From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:14:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship kissfft's BSD-3-Clause LICENSE in the wheel's
 dist-info

cmake/kissfft.cmake FetchContent-downloads mborgerding/kissfft at build
time (the repo carries no kissfft source of its own) and links its
kiss_fft.c/kiss_fftr.c objects, built KISSFFT_STATIC with
POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE, straight into libkaldi-native-fbank-core -
the shared library every wheel ships. Both compiled files, and the
_kiss_fft_guts.h/kiss_fft.h/kiss_fftr.h headers they pull in, carry
`SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause`.

setup.py declares no `license_files`, so setuptools' default
LICEN[CS]E* root glob is what ships kaldi-native-fbank's own LICENSE
(Apache-2.0); it never reaches kissfft's text, which isn't even in the
checkout to glob - it lands in the build tree only after CMake's
FetchContent runs. Reproduced against the real
kaldi_native_fbank-1.22.3-cp312-cp312-manylinux2014_x86_64.manylinux_2_17_x86_64.whl
from PyPI: dist-info/licenses/ carries only LICENSE.

Restoring kissfft's licence text (COPYING + LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause from
mborgerding/kissfft, copyright Mark Borgerding, unchanged since 2010)
at the project root as LICENSE.kissfft is picked up by that same
default glob with no packaging change, landing it in
dist-info/licenses/ alongside kaldi-native-fbank's own LICENSE.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; no fork of csukuangfj/kaldi-native-fbank to push from]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.kissfft | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.kissfft

diff --git a/LICENSE.kissfft b/LICENSE.kissfft
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7e9dc90
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.kissfft
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
